{%- comment -%}
  fye-profile-icon — a plain band's profile, photographed.

  Added 05/09/2026. For the matchmaker's profile step on the plain wedding ring
  journey.

  WHY A PHOTOGRAPH HERE AND A DRAWING FOR STONES. A stone's identity is its
  material, which a photograph of a ring cannot isolate — so stones are drawn
  (fye-gem-icon). A profile's identity is its geometry, and these images show
  it twice over: the cut band, and its cross-section beside it. That second
  element is the one that actually answers the question, and it is why a plain
  product shot would not do.

  Cut from one strip at native scale through a shared vertical window, so all
  nine rings are the same size and sit on the same line. That matters more than
  it sounds: a ring drawn 5% larger reads as a wider ring, which is a different
  question.

  USAGE
    {%- render 'fye-profile-icon', name: 'Traditional Court', class: 'rfd__oicon' -%}

  240x240 WebP, about 4KB each, white ground (not transparent — the tile ground
  is white, and keying the white out of a photograph with white highlights
  leaves halos on the metal).

  An unrecognised name renders NOTHING rather than a broken image, so a typo in
  the theme editor shows as a tile with its label alone.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign key = name | strip | downcase | replace: ' ', '-'
  comment
    The store's filter value is "D Shape"; the photography was labelled
    "D-shape". Both arrive here as d-shape, but Engagement Match is sometimes
    typed with an ampersand, so normalise that too.
  endcomment
  assign key = key | replace: '&', 'and'

  assign known = 'traditional-court,slight-court,d-shape,flat,flat-court,edged-court,edged-flat-court,engagement-match,concave' | split: ','
  assign ok = false
  for k in known
    if k == key
      assign ok = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign file = 'fye-profile-' | append: key | append: '.webp'
-%}
{%- if ok -%}
  <img class="fic fic--profile fic--profile-{{ key }} {{ class }}"
       src="{{ file | asset_url }}"
       alt=""
       width="240" height="240"
       loading="lazy" decoding="async">
{%- endif -%}
